  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 408 AM EDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nModel solutions show relatively good consensus consensus in having a \nreturn to a wetter pattern with moisture surging across SoFlo. \n\nThe synoptic setup will be dominated by an upper-lvl trough \ndeepening over the E/SE CONUS, with a series of shortwave energy \nimpulses traveling along its base. Moisture and instability will \nincrease as these features move across the state during the weekend \nand into early next week, promote shower and thunderstorm activity. \nThe unsettled weather pattern will also remove the SAL capping over \nSoFlo starting on Saturday. NBM and the rest of the long term \nguidance depict a trend of increasing chances of rain with a surge \nin POPs into the 60-80% range north of I-75, and 40-60% elsewhere on \nSaturday, and with increasing support for strong afternoon storms. \n\nThe unsettled weather continues on Sunday and Monday with a gradual \ntransition from westerly to southerly winds, then becoming easterly \nby Tuesday as the W Atl ridge expands across the area. This will \nshift the best chances of rain from eastern/interior areas during \nthe weekend to western areas by mid week. All in all, an active \nweather pattern will dominate the long term with much deeper \nmoisture filtering into the area and increasing mid/upper lvl \nsupport for stronger storms.   \n\nTemperatures will remain above normals, with highs generally in the \nlow to mid 90s, and morning lows in the mid 70s over inland South FL \nto around 80 closer to the coasts.",
